\caption{Buildability criteria. (a) Plastic collapse of the bottom layer when the self-weight added by each layer outpaces the growth of the static yield stress during printing. (b) Elastic buckling of a slender free wall. (c) The feasible layer cycle time lies between the stability requirement and the open time. \aidisclosure}
\label{fig:criteria}
\end{figure}

\begin{figure}[t]
\centering
\includegraphics[width=0.55\textwidth]{fig_rfail.pdf}
\caption{Empirical collapse-ratio distribution for published stack-to-failure tests. The calculator uses this distribution as an indicator alongside the physical assessment.}
