183: \subsection{Tool registry and schema projection}
184: 
185: Each tool is registered with its name, description, argument schema, executable function and access or runtime flags. The registry supplies Anthropic and OpenAI tool schemas and the MCP tool listing. Table~\ref{tab:tools} lists the \nnTools{} tools. Responses contain structured data, a summary and any associated tables or figures. Large responses are shortened for the model, while complete artifacts remain available to the user.
186: 
187: Input normalisation renormalises binder fractions to one with a warning and interprets admixture dosage as product mass relative to binder mass. Curing descriptions map to predefined conditions. An unrecognised material class returns an error with nearby valid classes for correction.
